It is Friday evening and the air is still very warm.
Someone knocks on my door.
I open up, and Sabine is standing there with her small dog Bruno.
"Happy birthday, Maya!", Sabine says and gives me a small houseplant.
"Thank you very much, Sabine, the plant is beautiful," I say.
They come into the flat.
We sit by the open window and enjoy the evening breeze.
Bruno lies quietly on the floor.
"How was your day at the office?", Sabine asks.
"Did you have a nice birthday?"
"Yes, the morning was a big surprise," I answer.
"I really had no idea."
Sabine smiles and pets Bruno.
"That was very nice of your colleagues," she says.
"Yes, the cake was delicious and we had a lot of fun," I explain.
I look at my new plant and feel happy.
